<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Intentionally empty.

	     This project is signed by a free Apple team, whose provisioning
	     profiles last 7 days. Any restricted entitlement (App Sandbox,
	     application-groups, keychain-access-groups, application-identifier)
	     must be authorized by a profile, so a distributed build carrying one
	     stops launching when that profile expires — AMFI refuses to spawn it
	     and the widget renders as an empty black rectangle. That is what broke
	     the 1.0.1 release seven days after it was built.

	     Shipping with no restricted entitlements and no embedded profile keeps
	     the app launchable indefinitely.

	     The host is also deliberately UNSANDBOXED, which is what lets it write
	     the shared state file into the widget extension's own container — the
	     only directory the sandboxed extension can also read. See
	     SharedPlayerStateFileStore. Network access needs no entitlement outside
	     the sandbox.

	     Note the asymmetry: the *extension* must keep com.apple.security
	     .app-sandbox or macOS will not register it at all. Only the host drops
	     the sandbox.

	     Do not add keys here without checking that the build still launches
	     more than 7 days after signing. -->
</dict>
</plist>
